Z||000000||Spyro86SE||08-25-2000||12:19 AM||||can anyone help my comp. keeps reading egr valve is bad but i just put a new valve in but it keeps reading code 32 can anyone help all help would be appreciated.<P><BR>thanks<BR>mikey||||reg||9
Z||000001||mshill||08-25-2000||01:51 AM||||If it is constantly happening then it is either the EGR soleniod, or a vacuum leak between the soleniod and the EGR valve.<P>If it only happens intermittently (like 10 minutes at 70 mph) then you may have a leak in your EGR tube.  At least thats how my broken tube manifested itself.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||08-25-2000||05:47 AM||||I know this is going to get some negativity but my EGR woes went away not when I replaced the solenoid, not when I replaced the valve, not when I checked all the vacuum lines, but when I retarded the timing back to specs! I had advanced it a tad about 8 months back and it wasn't till last month I remembered that was the other thing I had done before I started getting code 32. I haven't gotten it since <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> So for arguements sake I'm sure someone will say the timing has NOTHING to do with the EGR system but what can I say...it worked for me! Check it! Also do a search Spyro86SE, believe me there's PLENTY of info about EGR here. Some censored <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gokart_sig_1.gif"> <P>Marc                     87GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||08-25-2000||08:02 AM||||On behalf of Spyro86SE Thank for the help guys.<P>(He posts his questions by using my computer, His isnt running yet)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycarsig.jpg">  <B>My 1985 2M4 Sport Coupe </B><P><BR><B>My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A></B>||||reg||14
